<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 5: </span>Quantitative evaluation of LD-ViCE on the FERV39K classification task for varying denoising inference steps (<math id="A3.T5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>) and gradient loss scales (<math id="A3.T5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>). Results are reported on 7,847 samples from the test set. Higher values of both parameters generally improve classification success, with a slight trade-off in perceptual quality. Best values are highlighted in bold. <math id="A3.T5.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{c}=55" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>55</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{c}=55</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.T5.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=5</annotation></semantics></math> were selected as optimal values for subsequent experiments.</figcaption>
</figure>
